          %title Ultrafilters
          %h1#ultrafilters Ultrafilters
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#categorytheoretic_interpretations"} Category-theoretic interpretations
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ultrafilters_form_a_monad"} Ultrafilters form a monad
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ultrafilters_and_coproducts"} Ultrafilters and coproducts
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#theorem_r_brger"} Theorem (R. Börger)
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ultrafilters_and_presheaves"} Ultrafilters and presheaves
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ultrafilters_and_codensity"} Ultrafilters and codensity
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ultrafilters_and_unbiased_boolean_algebras"} Ultrafilters and unbiased Boolean algebras
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ultrafilters_via_other_algebraic_theories"} Ultrafilters via other algebraic theories
              %li
                %a{:href => "#comphaus"} Algebras of the ultrafilter monad
              %li
                %a{:href => "#number_of_ultrafilters"} Number of ultrafilters
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            An
            %strong ultrafilter
            on a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            satisfying the axiom
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∀
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in F \;\Leftrightarrow\; \forall (B_1, \ldots, B_n \in F),\; \exists (x \in A \cap B_1 \cap \cdots \cap B_n) .
          %p
            This is the only axiom necessary; from this, you can prove that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            to be a filter, then we need add only the axiom
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi B
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in F \;\Leftrightarrow\; \forall B \in F,\; \exists x \in A \cap B .
          %p
            Or if we start by requiring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            to be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+filter"} proper filter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇐
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leftarrow
            half of this latter axiom.
          %p
            We may also define an ultrafilter to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+element"} maximal
            among the proper filters. This definition generalises from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %em on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            but an ultrafilter
            %em in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+filter"} prime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
          %p
            Using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is an ultrafilter if, given any subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            or its complement belongs to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is as a Boolean-algebra homomorphism from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            to the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\bot,\top\}
            of Boolean
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
          %p
            Given an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of a set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %strong principal ultrafilter
            (on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            consists of every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            belongs. An ultrafilter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is
            %strong fixed
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            of its elements is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+subset"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is the principal ultrafilter at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %p
            In contrast, if this intersection
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong free ultrafilter
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter+principle"} ultrafilter principle
            (a weak form of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+set"} infinite set
            has a free proper filter (such as the filter of
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinite+subset"} cofinite subset
          %p
            Free ultrafilters are important in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
          %h2#categorytheoretic_interpretations Category-theoretic interpretations
          %p There are in fact many interrelated ways of defining ultrafilters. We present a few here.
          %h3#ultrafilters_form_a_monad Ultrafilters form a monad
          %p
            For any set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U X
            be the set of ultrafilters on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta\colon X\to U X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi U
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]\subseteq U X
            to be the set of all ultrafilters containing
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mi U
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \in U U X
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(\mathcal{F}) = \{ A | [A] \in \mathcal{F} \}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            into a monad. This monad is traditionally denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
          %p
            The ultrafilter monad can also be described as follows. The 2-element set carries a unique structure of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
            internal to the category of sets. When thus cast in the role of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizing+object"} dualizing object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo =
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                  %msup
                    %mi Bool
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Bool
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi Bool
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set \stackrel{P = Set(-, \mathbf{2})^{op}}{\to} Bool^{op}) \; \; \dashv \; \; (Bool^{op} \stackrel{Bool(-, \mathbf{2})}{\to} Set)
          %p
            whose corresponding monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Bool
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo −
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool(P -, \mathbf{2})
            is canonically identified with the ultrafilter monad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codensity+monad"} codensity monad
            induced from the full embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Fin
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin \hookrightarrow Set
            of finite sets into
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/28/13/28-13.pdf"} Leinster
            for a full account, and some extensions.
          %h3#ultrafilters_and_coproducts Ultrafilters and coproducts
          %p Observe that the canonical map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo +
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta(X) + \beta(Y) \to \beta(X + Y)
          %p
            is an isomorphism (for, each ultrafilter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo +
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X + Y
            must contain exactly one of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            given by
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X \cap A: A \in U\}
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_r_brger Theorem (R. Börger)
            %p
              The endofunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              is terminal among endofunctors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \to Set
              that preserve finite coproducts.
          %p A topological proof of this fact has been given by Richter (see references).
          %p
            This gives one universal characterization of the ultrafilter endofunctor. This theorem implies that there is precisely one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            structure on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon Set \to Set
            is a monad which preserves finite coproducts, then the unique transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to \beta
            is a morphism of monads.
          %h3#ultrafilters_and_presheaves Ultrafilters and presheaves
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Garner"}> Garner, 2018
              \.) The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \to Set
              that preserve
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+coproducts"} finite coproducts
              is equivalent to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
              of sets on the Blass category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U F
              of ultrafilters. The ultrapower functor with respect to an ultrafilter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              corresponds to the representable functor of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            The Blass category of ultrafilters has as objects, pairs of a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and an ultrafilter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{U})
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒱
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, \mathcal{V})
            are
            = succeed "-equivalence" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} =_{\mathcal{U}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+function"} partial
            continuous maps defined on a set in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in \mathcal{V}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(V) \in \mathcal{U}
          %h3#ultrafilters_and_codensity Ultrafilters and codensity
          %p
            Another known universal characterization of the ultrafilter monad is via the concept of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codensity+monads"} codensity monads
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"} Tom Leinster
            at the categories list, but it also appears sparsely in the literature; see for instance
            = succeed "," do
              %em Algebraic Theories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi Fin
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: Fin \to Set
            be the usual full inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            into sets. The restricted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mi Set
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi i
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mi Fin
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \stackrel{y^{op}}{\to} (Set^{Set})^{op} \stackrel{(Set^i)^{op}}{\to} (Set^{Fin})^{op},
          %p
            taking a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            contravariantly to the functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set(X, i-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mi Fin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mi Fin
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{Fin}(-, i): (Set^{Fin})^{op} \to Set
          %p
            (Note: this construction is dual to the familiar
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Kan construction
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Kan+construction"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: A \to C
            from a small category to a cocomplete category, and produces as output an adjoint pair whose right adjoint is a functor
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to Set^{A^{op}}
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
          %p
            The composite of these functors gives a monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \to Set
            which in fact is just the ultrafilter monad:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mi Fin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi i
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi i
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \cong Set^{Fin}(Set(X, i-), Set(1, i-))
          %p
            One way of considering the codensity monad formulation is that the ultrafilter functor is terminal among endofunctors whose restriction to the category of finite sets is the identity functor. This likewise gives the uniqueness of the monad structure, as well as the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is the terminal monad that restricts to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi Fin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{Fin}
          %h3#ultrafilters_and_unbiased_boolean_algebras Ultrafilters and unbiased Boolean algebras
          %p
            The codensity monad description is related to the traditional description in terms of Boolean algebras; to see this more clearly, it helps to pass to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} unbiased Boolean algebras
          %p Recall that an unbiased Boolean algebra is a product-preserving functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Fin
                    %mo +
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin_+ \to Set
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Fin
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin_+
            is the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is any set, there is an unbiased Boolean algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Fin
                    %mo +
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set(X, i_+ -): Fin_+ \to Set
          %p
            which may be called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em unbiased power set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Fin
                    %mo +
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_+: Fin_+ \to Set
            denotes the standard inclusion.) We may denote this by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^X
            for short. The inclusion functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_+
            is identified with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              An
              %em ultrafilter on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^X \to (-)^1
              in the category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Prod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Fin
                        %mo +
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prod(Fin_+, Set)
          %p
            Of course this is the same as a natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^X \to (-)^1
            in the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Fin
                          %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{Fin_+}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi i
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi i
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set(X, i-) \to Set(1, i-)
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mi Fin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{Fin}
            used in the codensity monad description of ultrafilters.
          %h3#ultrafilters_via_other_algebraic_theories Ultrafilters via other algebraic theories
          %p
            There are other descriptions of ultrafilters, based on
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Boolean+algebra#PostAlg"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                \-valued Post algebras
          %ul
            %li
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_k
              be the monoid of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctions"} endofunctions
              on a
              = succeed "-element" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq 3
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi BoolAlg
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi k
                    %mtext -
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_k: BoolAlg \to M_k\text{-}Set
              is full and faithful.
          %p
            Let us take for example
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 3
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_3
            takes the unbiased Boolean algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set(X, i_+ -)
            to the set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mn 3
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set(X, 3) = 3^X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set(3, 3) = M_3
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set(X, i_+ -) \to Set(1, i_+ -),
          %p
            to a morphism of
            = succeed "-sets" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_3
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 3
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set(X, 3) \to 3.
          %p The proposition implies that the mapping
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 3
                  %mtext -
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mn 3
                    %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta(X) \to M_3\text{-}Set(3^X, 3)
          %p
            is a natural bijection, giving us another way of viewing ultrafilters on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em unary
            operations.
          %p This is of course another codensity monad description in disguise; this time the codensity monad is induced by the full inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B M_3 \to Set
          %p of the category of endofunctions on the 3-element set into the category of sets. The results of this section say that the ultrafilter monad is the codensity monad for this particular inclusion.
          %p
            In a post to the categories list (see references),
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"} Bill Lawvere
            remarks that large cardinal hypotheses can be formulated as obstructions to similar codensity monads being isomorphic to the identity. For example, the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sets"} infinite sets
            is equivalent (assuming the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter+principle"} ultrafilter principle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is not isomorphic to the identity. Or, for the full inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{\mathbb{N}} \to Set
          %p
            the existence of an uncountable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+cardinal"} measurable cardinal
            is equivalent (in ZFC) to the fact that the induced codensity monad is not isomorphic to the identity (i.e., the first uncountable measurable cardinal is where the first “jump” takes place). Lawvere gives a couple more examples of a more geometric nature.
          %h2#comphaus Algebras of the ultrafilter monad
          %p
            A theorem due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernest+Manes"} Ernest Manes
            is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            of ultrafilter monad is the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
            with its obvious forgetful functor to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In one direction, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a compact Hausdorff space, then the corresponding algebra structure
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo :
                      %mi β
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi: \beta X \to X
              %p
                sends an ultrafilter
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to the unique point in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                converges. (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                %strong converges to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                if the filter of neighborhoods of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                is contained in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+space"} convergence space
            %li
              %p
                In the other direction, given an algebra structure
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ξ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi β
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi\colon \beta X \to X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq X
                to be
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open
                if
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi β
                          %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                      %mi and
                      %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{x \in X} \forall_{F \in \beta X} (x \in U \: and \: \xi(F) = x) \Rightarrow U \in F
              %p
                The sense of this is that a set is open if it is a neighborhood of each of its points, and the neighborhood filter of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                is the intersection of all ultrafilters that converge to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi prin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi (prin(x)) = x
              %p
                so that the neighborhood filter of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                is contained in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi prin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin(x)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                contains
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compactness
                is equivalent to having every ultrafilter converge to some point, and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorffness
                to having that point be unique.
          %p
            In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta X
            can be equipped with a compact Hausdorff topology which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            compact Hausdorff space generated by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone-%C4%8Cech+compactification"} Stone-Čech compactification
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topology"} discrete topology
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            also extends to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rel
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel
            of sets and binary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategories"} generalized multicategories
            defined relative to this extension can be identified with arbitrary
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relational+beta-module"} relational beta-module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            are to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategories"} multicategories
          %p
            By exploiting the connection between monads and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theories
            %strong compact Hausdorff object
            in any category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with small products, as a product-preserving functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Kl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi β
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Kl(\beta)^{op} \to C
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Kl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Kl(\beta)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            (or the full category of compact Hausdorff spaces whose objects are of the form
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
          %h2#number_of_ultrafilters Number of ultrafilters
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are principal and the number of them is the cardinality of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+set"} infinite set
            of cardinality
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{2^\kappa}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/independent+family+of+sets"} independent family of sets
